1
00:00:33,085 --> 00:00:40,698
I slide the wooden shutter wide,
The sleeping giant stirs inside.

2
00:00:40,888 --> 00:00:55,166
The heavy bellows draw their breath,
Defeating silence, conquering death.

3
00:01:02,970 --> 00:01:09,612
I press a single, high, clear key,
A tiny star for all to see.

4
00:01:10,173 --> 00:01:24,647
It floats like dust through arches high,
A whisper in a stony sky.

5
00:01:39,474 --> 00:01:46,431
I pull the registers all out,
The bass begins to roar and shout.

6
00:01:46,845 --> 00:02:01,352
The heavy Bourdon starts to growl,
Like some celestial, waking owl.

7
00:02:01,635 --> 00:02:08,871
The Jarre-fans turn their heads around,
Spellbound by this holy sound.

8
00:02:08,964 --> 00:02:24,016
The trumpet cuts just like a sword,
As I unleash my cosmic Lord.

9
00:02:38,370 --> 00:02:45,161
Cosmos and cathedral meet,
Laid out at the lion's feet!

10
00:02:45,481 --> 00:02:59,722
This is no mass, it is a flight,
A laser cutting through the night!

11
00:03:00,085 --> 00:03:07,435
I am not weeping, I am free,
Riding on a galaxy!

12
00:03:07,557 --> 00:03:21,751
Let the pipes and synths collide,
No more secrets left to hide!

13
00:03:36,727 --> 00:03:43,944
I weave the magic Bach lines in,
To let the space-age dance begin.

14
00:03:44,042 --> 00:03:58,317
Arpeggios climb like rockets high,
Breaking through the vaulted sky.

15
00:03:58,647 --> 00:04:05,652
Sequencers pumping in my wrist,
Rising up above the mist.

16
00:04:06,288 --> 00:04:20,403
A tsunami of light and sound,
Shaking up the holy ground.

17
00:04:20,663 --> 00:04:27,753
I’m playing Luna’s gentle smile,
Sending love down every aisle.

18
00:04:28,018 --> 00:04:42,645
I’m playing every kiss we shared,
And how she stood and how she cared.

19
00:04:42,739 --> 00:04:49,889
The final note begins to die,
A fading star up in the sky.

20
00:04:50,019 --> 00:05:04,719
The silence is so full and deep,
The singing lion falls to sleep.

